0..78 Comment "// Definitions a Rust caller runs on values of its own, through the runtime as"
79..92 Comment "// a library."
93..95 Comment "//"
96..174 Comment "// This is the boundary\'s first direction: Rust holds the composed program and"
175..250 Comment "// calls a definition by name. Nothing crosses by layout yet. Each argument"
251..304 Comment "// and answer is a value the runtime holds as itself."
305..307 Comment "//"
308..384 Comment "// The Rust test composes this source, names each definition and calls it on"
385..464 Comment "// integers it builds, then reads the answer back. Each `runs` item below makes"
465..525 Comment "// the same call from gandr, so both sides state one answer."
526..528 Comment "//"
529..607 Comment "// - see: #2901 — not implemented: values crossing by Rust\'s default layout,"
